("l-huet", "Domaine Huet", "estate", "Estate (Vouvray)", "Vouvray",
 "Founded by Victor Huet in 1928, made famous by his son Gaston, mayor of Vouvray, the estate owns three great vineyards: Le Haut-Lieu, Le Mont and Clos du Bourg. Under Noël Pinguet, Gaston's son-in-law, it converted to biodynamics in 1990. Its sweet and dry Chenins age for decades.", None),
("l-foreau", "Domaine du Clos Naudin", "estate", "Estate (Vouvray)", "Vouvray",
 "The Foreau family's Clos Naudin is one of Vouvray's most respected estates. Philippe Foreau makes dry, demi-sec, moelleux and sparkling Chenin according to the vintage and ages bottles for years in tuffeau caves.", None),
